<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Magersfontein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Magersfontein was fought on 11 December 1899 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kimberley">Kimberley</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piet-cronje">Piet Cronjé</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koos-de-la-rey">Koos de la Rey</a>, dug into trenches at the foot of the hills, repulsed a British attack under Lord Methuen. The defeat, which fell in the 'Black Week' of British reverses, halted the first attempt to relieve the siege of Kimberley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-magersfontein.jpg" alt="Battle of Magersfontein" width="278" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_in_Barbed_Wire_Magersfontein.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the Second Boer War the Free State mobilised its commandos alongside the Transvaal from October 1899, besieging Kimberley and Ladysmith and fighting at <b>Magersfontein</b> and Paardeberg.</blockquote><a href="/empire/orange-free-state">Orange Free State · Military</a></li></ul></section>
